          "kicker": "Selection hopes",
          "heading": "Bristol's Harry Randall says he 'can't pick' himself for England squad",
          "body": "Bristol Bears scrum-half Harry Randall, 28, wants back into the England squad, telling the club website: \"I'd love to get back in the England squad. I'd love to go to a World Cup. But, ultimately, I can't pick myself.\" Planet Rugby reports he is unlikely to make the upcoming Nations Championship squad, with Jack van Poortvliet, Ben Spencer, Alex Mitchell and Archie McParland all ahead of him in the pecking order. Bears director of rugby Pat Lam says Randall is in the \"form of his life\"."
