          "kicker": "Club takeover",
          "heading": "London Irish club target Championship return next season under Steve Daniels",
          "body": "London Irish, the club inactive since going into administration in June 2023, hope to return to professional rugby as early as next season. New owner and chairman Steve Daniels has vowed to put the club \"firmly back on the rugby map\" after Gamechanger Investments bought the name, brand and intellectual property from Kyle Jordan and Daniel McKeown. Chief executive Jamie Balls says the club would like to join the Championship at the earliest opportunity and would otherwise wait another year."
