          "heading": "Freddie Thomas, left out of Wales squad, scores decisive try for Gloucester",
          "body": "At Kingsholm, Gloucester beat Bath 23-5 in a Gallagher Premiership derby, and Freddie Thomas scored a decisive try with 18 tackles and 18 carries. The 24-year-old has played mostly blindside flanker this season rather than lock, and was left out of Steve Tandy's latest Wales squad. Gloucester are top of the Gallagher Prem, and Wales centre Max Llewellyn also crossed for the winners."
