          "heading": "Teddy Wilson earns Wallabies call-up as son of 1999 World Cup winner",
          "body": "Scrum-half Teddy Wilson has been named in Les Kiss' 33-man squad for the November Nations Championship Tests, with prop Tom Lambert one of the two new faces. Wilson is the son of David Wilson, who won 79 caps and was in the 1999 World Cup-winning side. The Guardian reports Wilson will push Tate McDermott for back-up to Ryan Lonergan, who has established himself as the standout No. 9. Wilson says his father \"just lets me play my game\"."
