          "kicker": "Centenary Test",
          "heading": "Japan's centenary Test slips 34-28 to Fiji as Volavola's late penalties decide",
          "body": "Japan's centenary celebrations in Tokyo ended with a 34-28 defeat to Fiji, who avenged their Pacific Nations Cup final loss to the Brave Blossoms. The sides were level at 21-all at half-time, with both teams scoring three converted tries. Fiji retook the lead through Terio Tamani's 44th-minute try, and Japan levelled at 28-all before veteran Ben Volavola kicked two penalties in the 60th and 69th minutes."
        },
        {
